  "rules": [
    "Every month reads its own list by day of the month; Adar of a common year reads Adar.",
    "A leap year: Adar I reads leapReview (the review of the laws of blessings and prayer, Hebcal's Adar II option B), and its 30th day reads nothing; Adar II reads Adar, so Purim's and Pesach's simanim come before their festivals. Hebcal reads Adar in Adar I and the option in Adar II; the source suggests starting the option on 23 Adar I.",
    "A short Kislev (29 days): its 29th day reads days 29 and 30 together.",
    "A long Cheshvan: its 30th day reads nothing. 15 Elul reads nothing (the luach's Klalim, which Sefaria's text does not hold).",
    "Hebcal's Adar II option A (the laws that depend on the Land, from the back of the Blum edition) is not in Sefaria's text and is not used."
  ],
